Tool sets for the Claude bar, `ask` and ultimate-mcp
====================================================

Every *.py file in this directory adds tools that Claude can use when you ask
it something from the Claude bar (Meta+Space), `ask`, or Claude Code through
ultimate-mcp. Packages install their files here (ultimate-redcyfer, for
example); nothing else needs changing.

A file is a Python module with:

    TOOLS = [fn, ...]
        Plain functions. The docstring's first part says what the tool does;
        its "Args:" section describes each parameter. Parameters have type
        annotations (str, int, float, bool). Each returns text.

    INSTRUCTIONS = "..."            (optional)
        A sentence or two telling Claude when to use these tools.

Rules
  * Read-only. Look, never change: no writes, no restarts, no requests that
    modify anything. The Claude bar promises that nothing it runs changes
    the machine or anything else.
  * Bound your time. Use ultimate_claude.plugins.run(argv, timeout=...) for
    commands; give network calls a short timeout.
  * Names are global: a tool whose name is already taken is skipped.
  * A file that fails to import is skipped with a warning; the built-in
    tools always load.

Example (/usr/lib/ultimate/mcp.d/example.py):

    from ultimate_claude.plugins import run

    INSTRUCTIONS = "For questions about the backup job, use backup_status."

    def backup_status() -> str:
        """When the nightly backup last ran and whether it succeeded."""
        return run(["systemctl", "status", "--no-pager", "backup.service"])

    TOOLS = [backup_status]
